        "orario": "13:35",
        "timestamp": 1773750935,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Lebanon: In the Bekaa Valley, a Christian village shelters displaced Shiite families Middle East Issued on: 17/03/2026 - 13:35 In eastern Lebanon, the Baalbek region – a stronghold of Hezbollah – has repeatedly been targeted by Israeli strikes since March 2. Fleeing the bombardment, residents from the predominantly Shiite area have sought refuge in the nearby Christian village of Deir al-Ahmar. FRANCE 24’s Laura Mousset travelled to this hilltop town overlooking the Bekaa Valley, around 100 kilometres northeast of Beirut, to witness this surge in solidarity. Guy Poran urges international community to demand Israeli govt end settler violence in West Bank 17/03/2026 Middle East Ghassan Salamé urges Israel and international community to let Lebanon 'do its job more efficiently' 17/03/2026 Middle East China overlooks Trump's demands for Hormuz strait, calls for all sides to de-escalate 16/03/2026 Middle East Israeli campaign in Lebanon seeks to 'degrade' Hezbollah’s rocket, drone and missile capabilities 16/03/2026 Middle East 'Near universal refusal' - European leaders reject Trump's demand for Strait of Hormuz mission 16/03/2026 Middle East Iran's underground arsenal, decentralised military key to press on with strikes on Gulf states 16/03/2026 Middle East Missiles and drone attacks across the UAE as Iran presses on with air campaign in Gulf 16/03/2026 Middle East Replay: Trump says US dismantled Iran's defense as Middle East war continues 16/03/2026 Middle East US allies 'know how to deal with Trump' amidst threats over Strait of Hormuz 16/03/2026 Middle East"
