        "orario": "13:32",
        "timestamp": 1773750750,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Guy Poran urges international community to demand Israeli govt end settler violence in West Bank Middle East Issued on: 17/03/2026 - 13:32 Modified: 17/03/2026 - 13:34 Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Guy Poran, former Israeli Air Force Pilot, human rights activist and volunteer for Israeli peace activist group Mistaclim. According to Poran, the situation in the West Bank has entered a dangerous phase, following wars in Gaza, Lebanon and Iran. He says the Israeli army is encouraging the escalating attacks by Israeli settlers, both passively and actively. To foster meaningful change, Poran is calling on the international community \"to raise hell\" and demand the Israeli government end the violence. Ghassan Salamé urges Israel and international community to let Lebanon 'do its job more efficiently' 17/03/2026 Middle East China overlooks Trump's demands for Hormuz strait, calls for all sides to de-escalate 16/03/2026 Middle East Israeli campaign in Lebanon seeks to 'degrade' Hezbollah’s rocket, drone and missile capabilities 16/03/2026 Middle East 'Near universal refusal' - European leaders reject Trump's demand for Strait of Hormuz mission 16/03/2026 Middle East Iran's underground arsenal, decentralised military key to press on with strikes on Gulf states 16/03/2026 Middle East Missiles and drone attacks across the UAE as Iran presses on with air campaign in Gulf 16/03/2026 Middle East Replay: Trump says US dismantled Iran's defense as Middle East war continues 16/03/2026 Middle East US allies 'know how to deal with Trump' amidst threats over Strait of Hormuz 16/03/2026 Middle East Israeli strikes hit southern Lebanese town 16/03/2026 Middle East"
